   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# sackview\n\nSee what\u2019s inside a ZIP archive before you unpack it. Each entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\n## Inspect an archive\n\nList the archive\u2019s entries and check the total unpacked size against your available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\n### Show the largest entries\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\n### Find entries by name\n\nShow only entries whose names match a pattern.\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\n## Your archive stays unchanged\n\nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive. Inspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service.\n\n## Supported format\n\nsackview supports ZIP archives only. Other archive formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code `24`.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) What does sackview show you?\n(b) What command lists the entries in photos.zip?\n(c) Does sackview extract files?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (c) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
